This is a big scope: server-side payment plan keys, prices, tier names, seat caps, case ceilings, lapse allowances, write allowance, migration, tests, ARB, mockup. The earlier business discussion established the new ladder. Rules say never implement future tasks early, but task 22 is open and this is a bug-fix/polish/plans revamp. Need to read docs/tasks/22*.md  [… 13,424 characters omitted] arate benefits card stay? The card design duplicates feature info (e.g., "Real-time cloud backup"). Keeping both is redundant and lengthens the page. The user asked for the card design; likely remove the separate benefits card or keep the gate explanation only. The sketch starts with "Choose the plan that fits your practice." and the toggle, then cards — no separate benefits card. So the plan should remove `_FeaturesCard` and `paywall_benefitsTitle` from the screen, or move its content into cards. But "Scope: only touch..." and the user's design implies removal. Need to confirm: remove the separate "Subscription Plans Offer" benefits card? The sketch doesn't have it. I'd propose removing it to avoid duplication, with the features now inside each card. Ask.

33. **Page title/subtitle**: The user's sketch says "Choose the plan that fits your practice." Is that the subtitle under the app bar title "Subscription Plans"? Or replace the title? Probably subtitle under the app bar. Keep app bar "Subscription Plans" and add the line. Need ARB. Or use as section header instead of "Plans". The sketch shows it then the toggle. Propose: app bar stays "Subscription Plans"; the line is the intro above the toggle.

34. **Where does the "reason" card go?** Keep `_LimitCard` above the intro when gate-opened. Fine.

35. **Server-side work vs UI-only**: The user asked "make a plan to implement this in the app." Does "this" include the full repricing/server? The card sketch uses new prices/tiers that don't exist. To make the app functional, yes. But the scope is large. We should present a phased plan: (A) data model + server, (B) UI cards, (C) tests/mockup/version. Ask what they want in this iteration: full repricing now, or UI-only against current prices? That's the biggest question. Since they've spent many turns settling the ladder, likely full. But the current task could be just the paywall UI redesign, leaving server pricing for later. However, the UI needs the new tiers and prices; can't show ৳60 Starter while checkout charges ৳100 Pro. So full.

Let me check the migration files for payment plan allow-list and tier definitions to scope the server work. Search `approve_payment`, `plan_type`, `subscription_plans`, `tier_ceilings`, etc.

Also, docs/tasks/22*.md and 00_INDEX. Let me locate.","open":false,"collapse":"preview"}
