So: fix the header to have title left, badge right, without overflow at large text. How to keep the badge right-aligned and avoid overflow at 1.5 with "Enterprise" + "Most Popular"? Options:
1. `Row` with `Expanded(title)` + badge; at large text the badge may still overflow. Use `Flexible` for badge + `FittedBox(scaleDown)` inside? That would shrink the badge text at large scale — acceptable? Previous overflow was 3px at 1.5 with title + badge row.
2. Row with title in Flexible (title text can wrap or scale) and badge fixed — title can wrap to two lines (title wraps naturally). Then no overflow: the title takes remaining width. Actually the 3px overflow: at 1.5 scale, "Enterprise" + "Most Popular" exceeded by 3px. If title is Flexible with allowed wrap, it wraps ("Enter\nprise"?) - words don't break; title is a single word "Enterprise" which cannot wrap → overflow persists. So wrap doesn't help for single-word titles. Hence the Wrap solution.

Better solution: keep Row, badge at the right, and let the title fit itself: `Flexible(child: FittedBox(fit: scaleDown, alignment: centerLeft, child: Text(title)))`. Then title shrinks if needed rather than pushing the badge off. Also badge could be in a FittedBox. The project already uses FittedBox elsewhere as the accepted remedy. This keeps the badge far right, at 2.0 line-height scale.

