ry is gone — and the three limitation bullets are **black** (`AppColors.secondary`) rather than error red. **(0.0.625, user request)** The three bullets carry the new wording — *Manage up to 50 cases at a time*, the cloud-feature sentence naming up to 20 associates, and *No cloud backup* — with the case count, the *No cloud backup:* lead and the offer's rates in bold. Below them the Free plan now shows **Want to Upgrade?** with the Starter per-month rates (3 months ৳60, 6 months ৳50, 1 year ৳45 — the last is why it says *starting at*) and a centred **Subscription Plans** button that opens the paywall. **(0.0.543, user request) A live paid plan can be cancelled from this page, and the ledger it leaves behind is Subscription History.** While a paid period is running and the plan is the account's own, the summary card carries a **Cancel** action at its right; a chamber member never sees it (their entitlement is the chamber's, and the RPC answers `firm_member`), and a free or lapsed plan has nothing to end. The confirmation window states plainly that a cancelled plan cannot be restored, with **Go Back** in black and **Confirm Cancellation** in red; confirming calls the server's `cancel_subscription()` RPC — the only writer of `subscription_cancellations` — which backdates the expiry behind the 48-hour grace and keeps the stored tier, then pulls the profile so the page reads **Pro — Lapsed** and shows its lapse allowance. The section formerly called **Payment History** is now **Subscription History**: `payment_submissions` and `subscription_cancellations` are read together under RLS, newest first and numbered as one list, and a cancellation is a card of its own carrying the plan and amount that were running, a red **Cancelled** label and the moment it happened. **(0.0.544, user request)** The **Cancel** action on the card is itself a filled red button with white text — the same red as the window's confirmation — rather than red text alone. **(0.0.545, user request)** The