mber.*; a chamber **member** gets the usage and the owner sentence instead of the two buttons, since the server refuses both actions for them. A firm **associate** can open **Subscription Plans** and read both tabs and every card, but each sellable action is greyed and a tap shows the toast *Only the firm owner can purchase a subscription for the firm. Please contact your firm owner to manage the subscription.* (`paywall_memberLockedToast`); the intro line and the free-limit gate card are not shown to a member. **Subscription History is not offered to a chamber member** anywhere in the menu, and the drawer's plans child is now offered to them as well. Supported by `test/features/subscription_details_screen_test.dart`, `paywall_screen_test.dart`, `accounts_profile_menu_test.dart` and `app_navigation_drawer_test.dart`. **(0.0.627, user request) The Cancel Subscription window takes the Exit App window's corner and grows.** Its corner is the same `AppSpacing.cardRadius * 2` (8 px), its side inset drops from the dialog default 40 px to 24 px (about 10% wider on a phone), its body gains 64 px of vertical room and its two actions are 53 px tall (10% above 48) — so the window is taller without a fixed height that would clip a longer Bengali line or a larger font. **(0.0.628, user request)** Its title is **middle aligned**, like the Exit App window's. **(0.0.640, user request)** A confirmed checkout no longer leaves the checkout beneath Subscription History: the post-submit navigation rebuilds the stack as the configured landing page → **Settings** → **Account & Profile** → **Subscription History**, so History's back button reaches Account & Profile, then Settings, then the landing page (read from `defaultLandingRouteProvider`). **(0.0.643, user report) An approval reaches the payer without a sign-out.** A free account deliberately holds no Realtime socket (sync is entitlement-gated) and there is no approval push, so after `approve_payment` the payer's app kept showing **Free** until launch, resume, reconnect or sign-in. The checkout now starts a bounded watch (`payment_approval_watch.dart`) after a confirmed submission: the account is re-read every **30 seconds for 10 minutes**, and the two ledger providers are invalidated on the same beat, so the plan, gates and Subscription History update while the payer waits. It pauses while the app is backgrounded (the resume refresh covers that), restarts on a second submission, and otherwise leaves later approvals to the ordinary launch/resume refresh. No server change. **(0.0.644, follow-up)** The early stop now captures the **governing expiry** — the profile's for an individual, the firm's for a chamber account, through the same `resolveSubscriptionExpiry` the entitlement uses — and ends the watch on the first successful beat where it changes, so a **renewal or queued plan change** stops as quickly as a free → premium approval. The free → premium check remains only as a fallback when the start could not be read; a failed refresh compares nothing. A rejected payment moves no expiry, so it still runs to the window.
