The cross is in, and I have the answer to the second question. Version **0.0.674**.

**The Review Note box now closes its own keyboard.** While the box is in focus (keyboard up), a cross appears in its trailing slot at the right of the box; tapping it closes the keyboard. It does **not** empty the box — the reason you typed is the review's own content, and a stray tap shouldn't wipe it. (The Login/Sign up Email box's cross does clear *and* unfocus, because a half-typed address is a query; this box holds content, so I kept the two jobs apart. Say the word if you want it to clear too.) The cross has an accessible name for screen readers: *Close Keyboard* / *কীবোর্ড বন্ধ করুন*.

**Why "Requested by:" says "A Firm Member".** That line reads **the phone's own profile cache**, not the server. A phone keeps exactly one profile row — the signed-in account's own — because the only place that writes one fetches *your own* profile, and `profiles` is not one of the tables the app syncs. A request row stores only the requester's account ID, so the name can't be read out of the row either. Concretely: `deleteRequestRequesterNameProvider` is a `ProfilesDao.getById` read ([delete_requests_viewmodel.dart](lib/features/settings/presentation/delete_requests_viewmodel.dart#L292)); the only writer of the local `profiles` row is `ProfileRepository.refresh`, which fetches `fetchProfile(currentUser.id)` ([profile_repository.dart:214](lib/features/accounts_and_profile/data/profile_repository.dart#L214) and [line 290](lib/features/accounts_and_profile/data/profile_repository.dart#L290)); and `profiles` appears nowhere under `lib/sync/`, so no colleague's row is ever pulled. The **Manage Firm roster** does show real names because it asks the server ([firm_repository.dart:915](lib/features/accounts_and_profile/data/firm_repository.dart#L915), allowed by the `profiles_select_self_or_firm` policy) — and the review screen makes no network call on purpose, because a review has to be workable offline.

So it is a **deliberate, previously-flagged choice**, not a bug — it was put to you in the Task 20 notes as *"the reviewer sees the requester's name best-effort and 'A Firm Member' otherwise… say the word"*, and it's still open. There are three ways to make the real name appear, and I changed nothing for this: (1) remember the roster's names on the phone when the roster is read, so reviews show them offline afterwards (the firm repository is touched); (2) carry the requester's name inside the delete request itself; (3) ask the server from the review screen when online, keeping the neutral fallback offline (inside Delete Requests, but adds a network read to it). Which you pick is a design call, so I've left it to you.

**Checks.** `flutter analyze` clean; [delete_request_review_test.dart](test/features/delete_request_review_test.dart) passes **16 cases**, the new one asserting the cross is absent while the box rests, appears on focus, closes the focus on tap and keeps the typed note — removing its `unfocus` call makes that case fail, so the assertion has teeth; full `flutter test` **2,148 passed**; version-log check clean, and its own test passes. No mockup owed.

Recorded in the plan, the [Task 20 file](docs/tasks/20_firm_management_and_delete_requests.md), the version log and [currentlyWorking.md](docs/currentlyWorking.md) — including the three options, so the ruling can be picked up next session.
