**What the reviewer sees.** Under **Awaiting Your Review** a card reads **Civil Appeal- 345/25** on the first line and **Case · Jannatul Ferdousi Rekha** on the second, where it previously read **Case · 26/10/2026**. The date has not been lost — it is still printed on the review screen itself, one tap away — so the queue now answers the question it is actually asked: who wants this record gone.

