Done — the server change is live and the app matches it.

**What happens now**
- **Someone else deletes the record:** every open request for it closes itself as **Already Deleted** in the same breath as the deletion. It leaves every reviewer's queue, stops counting in badges, and the requester's own list says what happened instead of "waiting". Nobody presses anything, and the only way to clear it is no longer to Reject it.
- **Someone else edits the record:** the review screen shows **As It Is Now** above **When the Request Was Made**, so Reconfirm is a decision about the version that exists. The old warning claimed the card below was what exists now, which was untrue; it is rewritten in sentence case.
- **The requester's side:** a **Changed** marker on their row while the record has moved, and the actions sheet explains that they can refresh the snapshot or withdraw.
- **Two people, one record:** a second request is refused with *A deletion request for this record is already open.*, and the server holds the same rule as an index.
- **Before editing:** opening the case form, Quick Update, the note editor, the reference sheet or a case-step dialog for a record someone else asked to delete warns **Requested for Deletion**, naming who asked and when — Continue Editing or Cancel. It warns, never blocks, and skips your own request.
- **A decision typed offline that loses its request** is adopted from the server instead of becoming a conflict.

**Proved on your project.** [delete_request_closure_test.sql](supabase/tests/delete_request_closure_test.sql) prints **CLOSURE OK** over six checks, all rolled back: a case deleted through the app's own door closes its request and stamps the deleter; a case step, note and reference close theirs; a parked request closes too; a duplicate is refused; an approval still ends **Approved**, not *Already Deleted*; the rule is internal and on all four tables. The one request already on your project (rejected) was left untouched, and the four triggers are live.

**Checks run.** [The migration](supabase/migrations/20261028100000_delete_request_target_closure.sql) applied and recorded (78 versions; ledger regenerated, guards moved to 78); `flutter analyze` clean; the delete-request, flow and push-worker suites 52 passed (new cases confirmed by name); `test/supabase/` 103 passed; case-form, case-detail, note and notes-todo suites passed after the editor change; version **0.0.685** recorded and the log check clean. Records are in [the plan](docs/implementation_plan.md), [Task 20](docs/tasks/20_firm_management_and_delete_requests.md), [currentlyWorking.md](docs/currentlyWorking.md) and the [Supabase README](supabase/README.md).

**Limits.** Nothing was run on a handset, so the warning window's feel is unverified on a real device; and I implemented "notify before editing" as a window on opening the editor rather than a banner inside it — say the word if you want the banner instead.
