 ### 12.5 The Shared Pop-Over Window Frame
 - **One frame for every centred window (0.0.705, user request).** The app's confirmation, choice and notice windows share one frame instead of each window drawing its own: an **8 px corner** (`AppSpacing.sheetRadius`, the Exit App window's), an **elastic width between 294 and 420 logical px** (the base width is 5 % above the original 280, user request 0.0.709; a short window stays at the base; a long title or body grows it only to the cap; the 40 px side insets stay the default and the Withdraw window keeps its 32, but when a pair would stack only because the margins leave it a few pixels short the side margins narrow — never below 16 px — until the row fits, 0.0.710), a **height capped at 85 % of the route's available height** with the body scrolling beyond it, and **112 x 48 / 16 pt actions with a 12 px gap**, centred. The actions adapt: a **pair sits on one line while both labels fit** at the active text scale, and becomes **two full-width buttons, one under the other**, when they do not; three actions keep their own grouping (the Invite Code window's Copy + Share with Close beneath), and windows designed stacked (Cancel Subscription, the paywall change/renew windows) stay stacked. **Contents do not move:** titles, bodies, fields, checkboxes, code boxes, rows, each window's own insets, title/body alignment (Exit and Withdraw keep centred titles; Withdraw keeps its justified body) and every action's label, order, colour and handler are the window's own.
 - **Where it lives.** `core/theme/app_dialog_metrics.dart` is the single source of truth (corner, width range, height factor, action size, gap, shape and the text/filled/outlined action styles). `shared/widgets/app_dialog_actions.dart` measures each label with `TextPainter.computeWidth` at the action's style, the active `TextScaler` and the ambient direction, and resolves row / stacked / wrap; the row falls back to a centred `Wrap` if a measurement is off, so an overflow stripe cannot appear. `shared/widgets/app_dialog.dart` builds it two ways over one rule: `AppDialogFrame` (and its `showAppDialog`, `showAppConfirmDialog` and `showAppNoticeDialog` entry points) around an `AlertDialog`, and `AppContentDialogFrame` around a plain `Dialog` for windows that draw their own body. The action plan is resolved in a `LayoutBuilder` **outside** the `AlertDialog`, because the dialog asks its subtree for intrinsic sizes and a builder inside it cannot answer; the 85 % cap rides in `AlertDialog.constraints`, because the route hands the builder tight screen constraints, so an outer constraint box cannot shrink anything. Action callbacks receive the dialog's own context, so a `pop` closes the window even if the caller's screen has since been replaced.
+- **The actions are the app's black or its error red, never another colour (0.0.736, user request).** Every light action kind now **states its own colours** in `AppDialogMetrics` instead of inheriting them from the global button theme: `text` and `outlined` are `AppColors.secondary` — the pure black `#000000` the rest of the app's buttons use — with an `onSecondary` white label (outlined keeps a black edge), and `primary` is the same black. The one colour this replaces is `AppColors.primary` (`#0F172A`, the ink navy), which was the only non-black fill in a window and read blue beside the app's black buttons; `destructive` keeps `AppColors.error` with `onError` white. A window's own `foreground`/`background` still wins (the paywall's explicit black pair is unchanged), and **no measurement moved**: the corner, the 294–420 px range, the 85 % cap, the 112 × 48 / 16 pt actions, the 12 px gap, the adaptive pair/stack rule and every inset are as they were. The pre-0.0.705 audit that came with the request found exactly one red action that had lost its fill — **Turn Off App Lock?**, whose Turn Off was red *text* — and it is now a normal destructive action; every other window that was red-filled before the shared frame (Delete Data, Delete Account warning, Manage Firm's confirmations, the admin reject and unconfirmed delete, the client-notification No, restore-replace, item delete, withdraw request, Cancel Subscription, `confirmDeleteDialog`) was already on the destructive kind and is untouched. Proof: the new colour case in `test/shared/widgets/app_dialog_test.dart` reads each kind's resolved fill and drawn label ink — text, outlined and primary are `AppColors.secondary`/`onSecondary` and explicitly **not** `AppColors.primary`, destructive is `AppColors.error`/`onError` — and `test/features/app_lock_test.dart` pins the Turn Off button's red fill and white label.
 - **For a new pop-over window (AGENTS.md rule 17).** Build it on the shared frame — `showAppDialog` / `showAppConfirmDialog` / `showAppNoticeDialog`, or `AppContentDialogFrame` when it draws its own body — and take every measurement from `AppDialogMetrics`. Do **not** create a local `AlertDialog`/`Dialog` frame, restate the corner, the width range, the height cap, the action size, the gap or the action colours, or keep a private copy of them. The window keeps its own title and body alignment, fields, rows, inner paddings, side inset and every action's label, order and handler; destructive actions use `AppDialogActionKind.destructive`, primary ones `primary`, outlined ones `outlined`. **The shared frame is a global surface:** its metrics, widgets, pair/stack/wrap rule, 294–420 px width, 85 % cap and adaptive margins change only when the user has asked for exactly that, never as a side effect of fixing one screen; such a change is recorded here and in Task 06 with its reason and proof. A window that genuinely cannot use the frame is a named exception below, with a comment in its code — so a later reader can tell a deliberate exception from an oversight.
 - **Waves.** **Wave 1 (0.0.705)** moved the **Exit App** window, the **Withdraw This Deletion Request?** window and **`confirmDeleteDialog`** (Case Detail, Case History and Notes deletes) onto the shared frame, with a narrow Exit case added. **Wave 2 (0.0.706)** moved the auth/account confirmations (logout's four windows, device removal, the Delete Data tick list, the Delete Account warning, Manage Firm's four confirmations, the Join a Firm plan warning, App Lock turn-off, the admin unconfirmed-account delete) and the settings/cases/sync confirmations (delete-request edit warning, raise, approve/reject and quick decision, the backup windows, the mobile-data update question, court/item deletes, the diagnostics channel choice, the client-number editor, the client notification prompt with its Remember footer, sync discard and export consent, the Paywall change/renew pair and Cancel Subscription) onto it. **Wave 3 (0.0.707)** moved the windows that draw their own body — Invite Code, Join a Firm, the firm rename, the backup/recovery passphrase, the edit-name window, the change-email password prompt and the Disposed help window — onto `AppContentDialogFrame`, the plain-`Dialog` variant that keeps each body byte-for-byte and adds the shared width range, 85 % cap and action area. **Wave 4 (0.0.708)** gave the bespoke windows the shared corner and width range (database recovery, print progress, the App Lock PIN pad), moved the admin reject note and its Add-Your-Own window onto the frame (their 96 px actions become the standard 112), and deleted the duplicated size/style constants, including the notification-time picker's. The deliberately unique windows keep their own frames: the date/calendar picker (360–460 px by design), Quick Update and the history-entry editor (480 px), the Settings pickers and the drawer account popover. **Component tests** (`test/shared/widgets/app_dialog_test.dart`) pin the 8 px corner, 280–420 width, the 420 cap on a wide screen, the 85 % height cap and scroll, 112 x 48 at 16 pt, the centred 12 px pair, the stacked pair at 320, the 360 px one-line pair that only fits after the margins narrow, the three-action grouping, the red destructive action, the returned answers and handlers, and a 2.0x text step.
 
